  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Combating trafficking through capacity building, training and sensitization of Police, Labour Officials, Anti Human Trafficking Units (AHTU) &amp; Prosecution</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project aims to strengthen and sustain anti-TIP partnerships, which have been initiated with various law enforcement agencies in the current running JTIP supported project (2010- Feb2013). This project will focus on prevalent forms of trafficking: child labor, bonded labor, sex slavery and forced marriages. It will provide legal and technical expertise, empower and build capacity of specialized newly initiated Anti Human Trafficking Units (AHTU) and facilitate inter-state police cooperation in 10 northern states, which are source areas for trafficking in India. It will focus on capacity building and training of prosecutors and it will strengthen Child Welfare Committees (CWC). The project will facilitate the sharing of information among law enforcement agencies in National Capital Region (NCR) of Delhi and the source areas for increased vigilance and cooperation to curb TIP while ensuring victims receive support and protection. The project will provide legal aid to victims while empowering and strengthening state legal aid institutions. It will create a 24x7 anti-trafficking response centre for technical and logistics support for interstate case interventions and ultimately integrate and institutionalize the centre into the governments tip response. The project aims to also to raise public awareness on trafficking.</narrative>
  </description>
